    "created_at": "2026-01-04T10:08:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T10:09:31Z",
    "body": "So this source file is uniquely fucked.\n\nSomehow it's otherwise valid file, but missing CompositionOffsetBox (ctts) which is supposed to contain some frame timing data.\n\nIt must have been muxed by something that either:\n  1. Didn't understand the H.264 stream had B-frames\n  2. Deliberately stripped the ctts for who knows what reason\n  3. Re-muxed from a source that already lost the timing info, e.g. broken camera / tv recorder or something\n\nTool tag shows Lavf60.3.100 tag suggests it was processed by FFmpeg/libavformat at some point, but FFmpeg normally writes ctts for B-frame content. So this is a mystery.\n\n\nWhat should smartcut do about this:\nI haven't fully decided yet. Probably we need to have some sort of fallback mode where we completely disregard the timing info in the source file and just recreate the timings from scratch.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
